\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces MAE by gameweek, against xP, on the population of Table~\ref {tab:predictor-mae}. Diamonds: validation MAE of the model chosen at each selection point (dotted verticals). Solid line: that model's test MAE on the gameweeks it was used for. Dashed line: the constant predictor. Gaps are gameweeks with no target.}}{54}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Deployed predictions against xP for every player-gameweek, gameweeks 6--38 without those lacking a target. Shading: number of player-gameweeks (log scale); dotted line: prediction equal to xP.}}{55}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces 2023-24: predicted points (solid), xP (dashed) and realised points (circles) of two players per position, drawn at random from those who played in at least 25 of the deployed gameweeks. Gaps are gameweeks without a target or a fixture. Each panel gives the player's MAE against xP.}}{56}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces 2024-25: as Figure~\ref {fig:pred-players-2324}.}}{57}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.5}{\ignorespaces Stage 1: standardised coefficients of the FantasyGo selection model by target gameweek, posterior mean and 94\% HDI, for the covariates chosen in at least 30\% of the gameweeks (at most four per position).}}{58}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.6}{\ignorespaces Stage 1: predicted against real share of the FantasyGo field for every player and round, gameweeks 6--38 (log scales; players picked by no entry are shown at $10^{-4}$). Shading: number of player-rounds (log scale); dotted line: equal shares.}}{58}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.7}{\ignorespaces Stage 1: the effect of $r$. (a) Season points; (b) season prize money; (c) mean standard deviation of the chosen team's points; (d) share of gameweeks in the top $1-r$ of the real contest, with MVT's mean estimated $\mathrm {Prob}\{Y_w>0\}$.}}{59}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.8}{\ignorespaces Stage 2: standardised coefficients of the league selection model by target gameweek, posterior mean and 94\% HDI, for the covariates chosen in at least 30\% of the gameweeks (at most four per position).}}{60}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.9}{\ignorespaces Stage 2: the retention coefficient $\gamma _m$ of the 132 manager fits (posterior means). (a) By position; (b) against the number of weeks of the manager's history.}}{61}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.10}{\ignorespaces Stage 2: out-of-sample check of the opponent model over the 28 gameweeks without a league-wide squad break. (a) Predicted probability of a player being in the opponent's squad against the observed share, in bins, for the players of the opponent's previous squad and for all others (log scales; dotted line: perfect calibration). (b) Rank, by predicted probability among the players the opponent did not own, of the 36 players the opponents bought (ranks above 60 shown at 60).}}{61}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.11}{\ignorespaces Stage 2, gameweek 9 at $r=50\%$: (a) estimated $\mathrm {Prob}\{Y_{w(\lambda )}>0\}$ over $\Lambda $, with $\lambda ^*$ marked; (b) predicted mean against standard deviation of the teams $w(\lambda )$.}}{62}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.12}{\ignorespaces Stage 2: cumulative points from gameweek 6 to 38 of MVT ($r=50\%$), the baseline, our real team and its real opponents, all scored with the same line-up rule.}}{62}{}%
